# Obsidian settings. Most of this folder is machine-local churn, but a few files ARE the
# vault's configuration: which plugins are on, where daily notes go, which template they use.
# Shipping those is the difference between "install two plugins" and a page of fiddly setup,
# so the folder is excluded and those specific files are added back.
#
# Deliberately NOT shipped: workspace*.json (your open panes, rewritten constantly),
# appearance/hotkeys/graph (personal taste), and plugins/ (the plugin code itself, which
# Obsidian downloads on its own).
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json
!.obsidian/core-plugins.json
!.obsidian/daily-notes.json
!.obsidian/templates.json
!.obsidian/community-plugins.json
.trash/
.smart-env/

# Never track credentials. If you add scripts later, keep their token stores out too.
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env*
!*.env.example
secrets.md
**/token_cache*.json
**/oauth_store.json

# Large binaries. Git does not diff them usefully and they bloat the repo forever.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mp3
*.zip

# Python, if you add scripts later. A virtualenv NEVER belongs in a synced or shared tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
